  <article class="article">
    <h1>About this site</h1>
    <p class="lede">The Gentle AI Guide exists for one reason: the people who could benefit most from AI are the ones nobody is explaining it to.</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Most writing about AI is aimed at experts, investors, or people who already use it every day. If you're not one of them, it can feel like the world changed while nobody showed you where the door is. This site is that door — calm, unhurried, and in plain English.</p>

      <h2>Who is behind it</h2>
      <p>The Gentle AI Guide is made by <strong>Jacob S. Olsen</strong>, an independent website publisher in Denmark. You can reach him any time at <a href="mailto:hello@gentleaiguide.com">hello@gentleaiguide.com</a> — questions from readers often become new articles.</p>

      <h2>How the articles are written</h2>
      <p>Honesty first: the articles on this site are written with the help of AI — the same kind of tool the site teaches you to use. Every article is then read, corrected and approved by a person before it is published, and each page shows the date it was last checked. The illustrations are also AI-generated, in one consistent style, and reviewed before use.</p>
      <p>We work this way on purpose. It's exactly the relationship with AI we recommend to you: let it do the heavy lifting, but never let it have the final word.</p>

      <h2>What we promise</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Plain English.</strong> Every technical word is explained the first time it appears.</li>
        <li><strong>No hype, no fear.</strong> We tell you what AI is genuinely good at and where it fails.</li>
        <li><strong>No pressure.</strong> Nothing here to buy, no account to create, nothing to install.</li>
        <li><strong>Your pace.</strong> Articles are written to be read slowly, and re-read.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>The site may in future carry a small number of clearly marked advertisements to cover its costs. They will never be disguised as articles, and no article will ever recommend a product because someone paid for it. See our <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> for what that means for your data.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
